Z||000007||84Bill||06-22-2001||09:49 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B>What is the length?<BR>(BTW, it IS an egg)<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I agree but it's not a dinosaur egg to the best of my knowledge. looks like an ostrich egg (due to the roundness of it) but I'm not an expert. <BR>If it smells like a rock it must be a rock but without tasting it one can't be sure    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>BTW congratulations on your find, I see the bottom picture you can see the shell and inner contents are different colors.<P><BR>Then again looking at it a bit harder and now that I know the size it's definatly not an ostrich egg. Dinosaur eggs are oblong in sshape but looking closely I can see it's 1/2 an egg.<p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 06-22-2001).]||||reg||12
